      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey i was watching the yen/usd charts earlier today while i was doing some deep focus work and something really weird happened. i was hyper-fixated on the way the candles were forming around a specific resistance level and i felt this sudden, heavy surge of mental clarity—almost like a rhythmic pulse in my head—and right at that exact millisecond the volatility spiked and broke through the level. it felt way too synchronized to be random noise. do you think there's any actual mechanism where high-frequency algo patterns can sync up with human cognitive rhythms or something like that??",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
